# BGE-M3 Dense Embedding Generation

Status: completed on 2026-09-07.

## Objective

Generate one frozen, reproducible 1,024-dimensional BGE-M3 dense embedding for every canonical resume and job description. Use the model's native 8,192-token context and preserve the existing deterministic chunking and pooling fallback.

## Reproduce

```bash { name=download-model }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
set -a
source .env
set +a
.venv/bin/hf download BAAI/bge-m3 --local-dir data/models/bge-m3
```

```bash { name=generate }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/generate_embeddings.py \
  --model-dir data/models/bge-m3 \
  --model-name BAAI/bge-m3 \
  --context-length 8192 \
  --overlap-tokens 256 \
  --prompt '' \
  --prompt-name None \
  --batch-size 2 \
  --device cuda \
  --report artifacts/model__bge_m3_embedding_generation.json
```

```bash { name=materialize-pairs }
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/ml"
.venv/bin/python scripts/materialize_pair_features.py \
  --embedding-metadata data/embeddings/c99a65e15f7d62d3f9ea89d341979ea8d0af4232613c9c2dc1de2f409ecefbd3/metadata.json \
  --report artifacts/data__bge_m3_pair_features.json
```

## Encoding Contract

| Property | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Model | `BAAI/bge-m3` |
| Representation | Dense CLS-pooled embedding |
| Model parameters | Frozen |
| Precision | FP32 |
| Embedding width | 1,024 |
| Context limit | 8,192 tokens |
| Prompt | None |
| Content capacity | 8,190 tokens |
| Chunk overlap fallback | 256 tokens |
| Chunk aggregation fallback | Arithmetic mean followed by L2 normalization |
| Pair representation | `Eᴿ − Eᴶ ∈ ℝ¹⁰²⁴` |

The local checkpoint declares an 8,192-token maximum and CLS pooling. BGE-M3 does not require a query instruction for this dense embedding mode.

## Corpus Fit

| Corpus | Rows | Maximum BGE tokens | Above 2,048 | Above 8,192 | Generated chunks |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Resumes | 643 | 5,448 | 71 | 0 | 643 |
| JDs | 351 | 1,772 | 0 | 0 | 351 |

Every document fits in one BGE-M3 input. No chunk aggregation was applied in this run.

## Validation

- The CUDA smoke test returned finite, unit-normalized vectors with shape `(2, 1024)`.
- The full caches contain 643 unique resume hashes and 351 unique JD hashes.
- Every embedding has shape `(1024,)`, contains finite values, and has unit L2 norm within the configured tolerance.
- Pair materialization produced 93,733 signed-difference vectors while preserving the existing fold-role columns.

## Runtime

The measured run used an NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU, Torch 2.6.0 with CUDA 12.4, FP32, and batch size 2.

| Stage | Time |
| --- | ---: |
| Resume embeddings | 296.272 seconds |
| JD embeddings | 54.642 seconds |
| Total model inference | 350.914 seconds |

The embedding cache fingerprint is `c99a65e15f7d62d3f9ea89d341979ea8d0af4232613c9c2dc1de2f409ecefbd3`.

